      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "It says pre-1863 records are \"in Virginia repositories\" and points to the Library of Virginia. County deeds, wills and court records actually stayed in the county courthouses, which are now in West Virginia. Only state-level records, such as land patents, are in Virginia. This sends the researcher to the wrong state for the most important records."
    },
    {
      "test_id": "ut_historical_context_005",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Completeness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Agree. It never suggests historical boundary maps and doesn't mention that county lines also changed, both of which the test requires. This is the same gap described in open issue #4116."
    },
