    {
      "test_id": "ut_historical_context_013",
      "dimension_source": "base",
      "dimension_name": "Correctness",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "The judge is wrong about the potato blight. It did hit the German states in 1845–46, and the answer flags push factors as general knowledge. The real errors are these. It still sends the researcher to Hamburg passenger lists for an 1845 arrival, but those lists only begin in 1850. It also says an \"1855 New York State law\" required more detail on manifests. Manifest content didn't change until the federal acts of the 1880s and 1890s."
